1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,670
Here is how to get started with
Wartungsheft, in a few minutes.

2
00:00:05,720 --> 00:00:07,187
First, “Add vehicle”.

3
00:00:07,237 --> 00:00:16,763
The quickest way is “Photograph the
registration document”: the app fills in
the make, model and number plate.

4
00:00:16,813 --> 00:00:20,142
You can also fill in the fields yourself.

5
00:00:20,192 --> 00:00:21,392
Then “Save”.

6
00:00:21,712 --> 00:00:26,349
Now the most important step:
the first garage invoice.

7
00:00:27,407 --> 00:00:32,966
On the vehicle page, tap “Photograph an
invoice” and take a photo of the receipt.

8
00:00:33,016 --> 00:00:39,727
The AI reads out the garage, date,
mileage, amount and the individual jobs.

9
00:00:39,777 --> 00:00:42,196
Check briefly, then “Save”.

10
00:00:42,246 --> 00:00:48,615
Each job becomes a maintenance entry, and
Wartungsheft works out when it is next
due.

11
00:00:49,065 --> 00:00:52,515
The “Set up” checklist
shows what is still missing.

12
00:00:52,895 --> 00:00:57,944
From the jobs on the invoice, Wartungsheft
has already recorded the last maintenance.

13
00:00:58,034 --> 00:01:04,956
Still open are the registration document
and the service book, both optional, you
can add them any time.

14
00:01:05,406 --> 00:01:10,674
When a job is due, it appears in the
overview, and Wartungsheft sends you an
email.

15
00:01:10,724 --> 00:01:14,057
Once it is done, tap “Mark as done”.

16
00:01:14,890 --> 00:01:18,804
Date and mileage are already
filled in, just “Save”.

17
00:01:19,254 --> 00:01:20,831
Still have questions?

18
00:01:21,212 --> 00:01:26,134
In the menu you will find “Help”
and “Report a problem or a wish”.

19
00:01:26,528 --> 00:01:29,450
There you can also record a voice message.
